    {
      "id": "L048",
      "kind": "ledger-row",
      "date": "2026-09-23",
      "title": "#342's criteria — hold React at 19.2.x because `@react-three/fiber`'s peer range excludes it — rested on an upstream fact that expired **~31 hours after the issue was written** (#342 created 2026-09-21T12:46:27Z; R3F 9.8.0 published 2026-09-22T19:43:58Z): `pmndrs/react-three-fiber#3916` merged 2026-09-22 and v9.8.0 widened `peerDependencies.react` to `>=19 <19.4`, so the issue's own documented lift condition was already satisfied before any builder opened it. Building it as written would have merged a pin whose stated removal condition was met, holding HACER back from a React release upstream supports. Fourth occurrence today of the class in `docs/harness/sessions/2026-09-23.md` §7",
      "source": "docs/harness/ledger.md:63"
    }
  ]
